        "Rearrange each line into $y=mx+c$.",
        "Multiply the two gradients.",
        "Perpendicular finite gradients have product $-1$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "The first line is $y=\\frac43x-\\frac{25}{3}$; the second is $y=-\\frac34x+\\frac{25}{4}$.",
        "Their gradient product is $\\frac43\\times-\\frac34=-1$.",
        "Therefore the tangents are perpendicular."
      ]
